  "notes": "The Aftermath staff producer, and the sourced fact is a *pedigree* that maps straight onto harmony: son of Chic's Bernard Edwards, \"which puts **functional harmony** in the palette: `ii7–V–Imaj7` cycles, `i–iv–VII–III` minor motion, and modulating bridges rather than 2-chord vamps.\" So this model is the least vamp-like thing in the lane — `borrowed.V` 0.40, 80% of `extensions` above the triad, `harmonicRhythm` weighted 5:2 to one chord per bar, and a `prechorus` in the form. The second sourced parameter is the inverse of every other entry here: \"the arrangement is **chord-first** and the melody sits inside the voicing\", which is `chordToneBias` 0.85 with `intervals.leap` 0.06 and `structure` `long_arc` — the melody is not allowed to be a hook fighting the chords. \"Disco-derived four-on-the-floor appears on the up-tempo material\" is authored literally as `kick.fourOnFloorInChorus`. Bass is played-style: \"walking, syncopated, melodic, with a sub layer beneath; portamento rare\" is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.42, `glideProb` 0.02, `anticipationProb` 0.40 and major-mode cell shapes. ⚠ `medium`: \"pedigree, role and credits documented; drum/tempo parameters largely inferred **[LOW-CONF]**\". The INFERRED parameters are the entire `drums` block and the `session.bpm` band — the research states a tempo span but no habit inside it. ⚠ The 130-140 half-time population is not modeled (one `halfTime` boolean, no modes authored). ⚠ Modulating bridges are documented and cannot be modeled: the engine holds one key per session, so the bridge is expressed as a section with its own rule instead. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.3 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.3 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 50 to 47 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 48 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3.",
